# cigar-butt — credential template.
#
# Copy to a file OUTSIDE the repository and point the server at it:
#
#   cp .env.template ~/.config/cigar-butt/env
#   export CIGAR_BUTT_ENV_FILE=~/.config/cigar-butt/env
#
# Or skip the file entirely and run the `setup_credentials` tool, which writes
# a 0600 JSON file under your config directory. Environment variables always
# win over that file, so you can override one key for a single run.
#
# Never commit a filled-in copy. `.env` and `.env.local` are gitignored;
# this template is the only credential file that belongs in version control.


# ─── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SEC EDGAR has no API key. It identifies callers by a descriptive User-Agent
# containing a real name and email. Without one EDGAR returns 403 and may block
# your IP. Rate limit is 10 requests/second.
# Docs: https://www.sec.gov/os/webmaster-faq#developers
SEC_USER_AGENT=Your Name your-email@example.com


# ─── Price data — at least one required ──────────────────────────────────────

# Tiingo. Split- and dividend-adjusted daily closes; the preferred source.
# Free tier: ~50 unique tickers/hour, 500 requests/day.
# Register: https://www.tiingo.com/account/api/token
TIINGO_API_KEY=

# Polygon.io. Whole-market daily bars in one call, delisted-ticker reference
# data, and corporate actions. Free Basic plan, no card.
# Free tier: 5 calls/minute, end-of-day data, ~2 years of history.
# Register: https://polygon.io/dashboard/api-keys
POLYGON_API_KEY=

# Alpha Vantage. Fundamentals cross-check and a last-resort quote. Too
# rate-limited to screen with — use it to sanity-check a finalist.
# Free tier: ~25 requests/day, 5 calls/minute.
# Register: https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=


# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# FRED (St. Louis Fed). Moody's Aaa corporate bond yield, which sets Graham's
# earnings-yield hurdle, plus CPI for real-return adjustment and the 10-year
# Treasury. Free, issued instantly. Required by `macro_context` and nothing else.
# Register: https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys
FRED_API_KEY=

# FINRA consolidated short interest needs NO credential and no entry here. It is
# used by `short_interest` to answer "why is this cheap?" with a fact.
# FDIC BankFind is likewise unauthenticated; `bank_call_report` just works.


# ─── Brokerage: E*TRADE (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only needed to pull live account balances and positions. Everything else in
# this server works without it.
#
# Read-only: this server never places an order.
#
# E*TRADE issues two independent key pairs and they are NOT interchangeable — a
# sandbox access token is rejected by production even if sent to the right host.
#
#   Sandbox keys      Self-service, instant, return canned data (ask for GOOG,
#                     get AAPL). https://us.etrade.com/etx/ris/apikey
#   Production keys   A separate flow on us.etrade.com: the API User Intent
#                     Survey, then the API Developer Agreement, then an annual
#                     market-data attestation. An individual key is displayed
#                     immediately on completing the survey and agreement — no
#                     email, no PDF, no phone call. Start at
#                     https://developer.etrade.com/getting-started
#                     An E*TRADE account is required but need NOT be funded to
#                     get a key; funding is only needed to trade. An individual
#                     key is locked to the user ID that created it.
#
# Which pair the server uses: 'sandbox' or 'production'. Both ETRADE_ENV and
# ETRADE_ENVIRONMENT are accepted.
ETRADE_ENV=sandbox

ETRADE_SANDBOX_CONSUMER_KEY=
ETRADE_SANDBOX_CONSUMER_SECRET=

# Production keys can place real orders against a funded account. Prefer the
# server's own 0600 credential file (via `setup_credentials`) or a keychain
# over a dotenv file that other processes can read.
ETRADE_PROD_CONSUMER_KEY=
ETRADE_PROD_CONSUMER_SECRET=

# Access tokens are written per environment by `broker_connect` into the 0600
# credential file — do not set them here. Storing both key pairs above lets the
# `broker_environment` tool switch between them; tokens are kept separate too,
# so connecting one environment never disconnects the other. E*TRADE tokens idle out after two hours (the server
# renews automatically inside that window) and die at midnight US Eastern, which
# nothing can renew past: after midnight, re-run `broker_connect`.


# ─── Server behaviour (all optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Point the server at this file. Without it, only real environment variables
# and the config-directory credential file are read.
# CIGAR_BUTT_ENV_FILE=~/.config/cigar-butt/env

# Override where credentials are stored. Default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cigar-butt/
# credentials.json, falling back to ~/.config/cigar-butt/credentials.json
# CIGAR_BUTT_CONFIG=

# Override the response cache location. Default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cigar-butt/
# cache.sqlite, falling back to ~/.cache/cigar-butt/cache.sqlite
# CIGAR_BUTT_CACHE=

# Bypass the cache entirely, for both reads and writes.
# CIGAR_BUTT_NO_CACHE=1
